2025-11-02 01:44:24,186 - hybrid_agentic_analysis - INFO - combined result: {'tracker': <dynamodb_tracker.DynamoDBTracker object at 0x10b5c5100>, 'input_config': InputConfig(project_name='Debug Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices'), 'project_config': ProjectConfig(project_name='Debug Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices', project_id='4fbd253f-9366-41c5-8de8-daa65df18de3', result_path=''), 'project_result': None, 'combine_phase': False, 'research_data': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1\r\nDate: March 15, 2024\r\nInterviewer: Research Team Member\r\nInterviewee: Alex Morrison (Pet Parent)\r\nDuration: 45 minutes\r\nPets: Agent Dale Cooper (Cat, 6 years old) and Audrey Horne (Dog - Golden Retriever, 4 years old)\r\n\r\nQuestion 1: Can you tell me about your overall approach to keeping Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey Horne healthy? What does pet wellness mean to you?\r\nResponse: Oh, that\'s such a big question to start with! For me, pet wellness is really about looking at the whole picture, you know? It\'s not just about making sure they\'re not sick - it\'s about them thriving and being happy. With Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey, I think about it in layers. There\'s the physical health aspect, obviously - making sure they\'re at a good weight, their coats are shiny, they\'re active. But there\'s also the mental and emotional side that I think people sometimes overlook.\r\nAgent Dale Cooper, being a cat, he needs different things than Audrey does. He needs mental stimulation through play, places to climb and perch, windows to look out of. He\'s very particular about his environment being just right. Audrey, on the other hand, she needs that social interaction, the physical exercise, the training that keeps her mind engaged.\r\nI guess my overall approach is preventative rather than reactive. I\'d rather invest time and energy into keeping them healthy than dealing with problems after they arise. That means regular vet visits, yes, but also daily observation. I know their normal behaviors so well that I can tell immediately if something\'s off. Like last month, Agent Dale Cooper was just sitting differently - nothing dramatic, but I could tell his posture was off. Turned out he had a minor muscle strain from jumping weird off the cat tree.\r\nI also believe in balance. I\'m not one of those pet parents who goes to extremes - I don\'t cook elaborate meals from scratch every day or anything like that. But I do research everything I give them, every toy I buy, every change I make to their routine. It\'s about making informed decisions that work for our lifestyle while prioritizing their wellbeing.\r\n\r\nQuestion 2: Let\'s talk about diet specifically. What do you feed Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey, and how did you decide on their current feeding routines?\r\nResponse: Diet has been quite a journey for us, actually. When I first got Agent Dale Cooper five years ago, I just bought whatever cat food was on sale at the grocery store. I didn\'t know any better. But then he started having some digestive issues - nothing serious, but enough that the vet suggested I look into higher quality food. That sent me down this whole rabbit hole of pet nutrition research.\r\nFor Agent Dale Cooper now, I feed him a combination of high-quality wet and dry food. In the morning, he gets about 3 ounces of wet food - I rotate between three different brands to give him variety. Right now, I\'m using brands that focus on high protein content with no fillers or by-products. The first ingredient is always actual meat, not meal or by-product. He gets salmon-based food twice a week because it\'s good for his coat, and chicken or turkey the other days. I tried duck once, but he looked at me like I\'d personally offended him and refused to eat it for two days.\r\nThroughout the day, he has access to dry food, but I measure it out - about 1/4 cup total. I learned the hard way that free-feeding without limits led to him gaining two pounds in three months. The vet wasn\'t happy about that. His dry food is a dental health formula because cats are prone to dental issues, and honestly, trying to brush Agent Dale Cooper\'s teeth is like trying to negotiate with a tiny, furry tornado.\r\nAudrey\'s diet is different because she\'s much more active and, being a Golden Retriever, she has different nutritional needs. She gets fed twice a day - morning and evening. I give her about 1.5 cups of high-quality dry kibble each meal, so 3 cups total per day. Her food is specifically formulated for active adult dogs, with glucosamine for joint health since Goldens can have hip issues later in life.\r\nI supplement Audrey\'s diet with healthy treats during training - things like small pieces of carrot, green beans, or these little freeze-dried liver treats that she goes absolutely crazy for. But I count those calories as part of her daily intake. I learned to do that after she gained five pounds one summer when I was doing a lot of training with her and didn\'t account for all those treats.\r\nOh, and water! I\'m obsessive about water. They both have multiple water stations around the house, and I change the water twice a day. Agent Dale Cooper has this fancy ceramic fountain because cats prefer moving water, apparently. Audrey just has regular bowls, but I have one inside and one outside because she\'s always running in and out.\r\nThe timing of meals is important too. Agent Dale Cooper gets his wet food at 7 AM and 6 PM like clockwork. If I\'m even five minutes late, he sits by his bowl and gives me this look of utter betrayal. Audrey eats at 7:30 AM and 5:30 PM. I feed them at slightly different times to avoid any food competition issues, even though they respect each other\'s bowls pretty well.\r\n\r\nQuestion 3: How do you handle exercise and physical activity for each of your pets? What does a typical day look like?\r\nResponse: Exercise routines are completely different for each of them, as you can imagine! Audrey is my marathon runner, and Agent Dale Cooper is more of a sprinter who believes in strategic energy conservation.\r\nLet me start with Audrey because her routine is more structured. We begin every single day with a morning walk, rain or shine. I wake up at 6 AM, and by 6:30, we\'re out the door. The morning walk is usually about 45 minutes to an hour, depending on the weather and my schedule. We have three different routes we rotate through to keep things interesting for her. One goes through the park where she can sniff all the good smells, another goes past the lake where she sometimes gets to swim in summer, and the third is more of an urban route where we practice her leash manners around distractions.\r\nAfter work, around 5 PM, before dinner, we do another activity. Three days a week, this is another walk, usually 30 minutes. But twice a week, we go to the dog park instead, where she can really run and play with other dogs for about an hour. Weekends are when we do our big adventures - hiking trails, beach trips if the weather\'s nice, or sometimes agility practice in the backyard. I set up some basic agility equipment - nothing fancy, just some jumps and weave poles - and she loves it.\r\nBeyond structured exercise, Audrey gets mental stimulation through training sessions. We do about 10-15 minutes of training every evening. Sometimes it\'s basic obedience reinforcement, sometimes we\'re learning new tricks. Right now, we\'re working on "tidy up," where she puts her toys back in the toy basket. She\'s getting pretty good at it, though she sometimes tries to cheat by just dropping them near the basket rather than in it.\r\nAgent Dale Cooper\'s exercise needs are totally different. Cats need short bursts of intense activity rather than sustained exercise. I do two dedicated play sessions with him daily - one in the morning after breakfast and one in the evening before bed. Each session is about 15-20 minutes, or until he starts panting or loses interest. I use different toys to simulate hunting behaviors - feather wands for bird-like prey, laser pointers for quick movement (though I always end with a physical toy so he can actually "catch" something), and these little fake mice that he likes to carry around.\r\nThe interesting thing about Agent Dale Cooper is that he\'s most active at dawn and dusk - classic cat behavior. So around 5 AM, I often hear him racing around upstairs, doing what I call his "morning zoomies." He runs from room to room, jumps on and off furniture, and generally acts like he\'s possessed for about 10 minutes. Then he\'s done and goes back to sleep. He does the same thing around 9 PM.\r\nI\'ve also set up the house to encourage natural movement for him. I have cat trees in three different rooms, shelves mounted on the walls to create climbing paths, and window perches where he can watch birds. He probably climbs up and down his various perches 20-30 times a day. I\'ve actually watched him sometimes, and he has favorite routes through the house that involve jumping from surface to surface without touching the floor - like the floor is lava or something.\r\nOne challenge is that Agent Dale Cooper is an indoor-only cat, so I have to be creative about exercise. I\'ve trained him to walk on a harness and leash, and we go out in the backyard sometimes, but he\'s not really into it. He mostly just sits and eats grass and glares at me for subjecting him to the indignity of a harness. But the indoor play sessions seem to be enough for him - he maintains a healthy weight and the vet says his muscle tone is good.\r\n', 'chunks': [{'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-1', 'content': 'Pet wellness is about the whole picture, not just preventing sickness but ensuring pets thrive and are happy.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'holistic approach']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-2', 'content': 'Physical health and mental/emotional wellbeing are both important aspects of pet wellness.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'physical health', 'mental health']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-3', 'content': 'Different pets have different needs; cats need mental stimulation and dogs need social interaction and physical exercise.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['cats', 'dogs', 'pet needs']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-4', 'content': 'Alex Morrison prefers a preventative approach to pet health, focusing on regular vet visits and daily observation.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['preventative care', 'pet health']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-5', 'content': 'Balance in pet care is important; making informed decisions without going to extremes.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['pet care', 'balance']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-6', 'content': 'Diet for pets has evolved from buying whatever was on sale to choosing high-quality, high-protein foods.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['pet diet', 'food quality']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-7', 'content': 'Agent Dale Cooper (cat) is fed a combination of wet and dry food, with a focus on high protein and no fillers.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['cat diet', 'food choice']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-8', 'content': 'Audrey (dog) is fed twice a day with high-quality dry kibble formulated for active adult dogs.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['dog diet', 'food choice']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-9', 'content': 'Healthy treats are used as supplements during training, with calories counted as part of the daily intake.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['healthy treats', 'training']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-10', 'content': 'Multiple water stations are set up around the house, with water changed twice a day.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['hydration', 'water stations']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-11', 'content': "Exercise routines differ significantly between Agent Dale Cooper (cat) and Audrey (dog), reflecting their species' needs.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['exercise routine', 'species differences']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-12', 'content': "Audrey's structured exercise includes morning walks, dog park visits, and agility practice.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['dog exercise', 'structured activity']}, {'id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-13', 'content': "Agent Dale Cooper's exercise involves short bursts of intense activity, with dedicated play sessions and natural movement encouraged by home setup.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['cat exercise', 'home setup']}], 'inferences': [{'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-1', 'meanings': ['Pet wellness encompasses both preventive measures against illness and the promotion of a fulfilling and joyful life for pets.', 'Wellness in pets is defined broadly, including their physical health, mental state, and overall happiness.'], 'importance': 'Understanding pet wellness in a holistic manner is crucial for providing comprehensive care that goes beyond mere survival to ensuring a quality life.', 'context': "This highlights a shift in pet care philosophy towards a more integrated approach, considering all aspects of a pet's life.", 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The statement emphasizes the importance of a broad perspective on pet health, suggesting that optimal care involves more than just preventing or treating sickness.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-2', 'meanings': ['Both the physical and mental/emotional health of pets are critical components of their overall wellness.', 'Acknowledging mental and emotional well-being as essential reflects an understanding of pets as complex beings with needs beyond the physical.'], 'importance': 'This underscores the necessity of a comprehensive approach to pet care, recognizing that neglecting any aspect of health can lead to problems.', 'context': 'It suggests a growing awareness and acceptance of the complexity of pet health, mirroring broader trends in human health and wellness.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The statement makes it clear that pet wellness is multifaceted, requiring attention to both physical health and mental/emotional well-being.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-3', 'meanings': ['Different species of pets have unique requirements for their well-being, highlighting the need for species-specific care strategies.', 'The specific needs of cats and dogs are highlighted, showing that what benefits one species may not be suitable for another.'], 'importance': 'This emphasizes the importance of tailored care approaches that consider the natural behaviors and preferences of different pet species.', 'context': 'This points to the complexity of pet care, where knowledge of species-specific needs is essential for promoting health and happiness.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'By specifying the needs of cats and dogs, the statement illustrates the necessity of understanding and catering to the distinct needs of different types of pets.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-4', 'meanings': ['Alex Morrison advocates for a proactive approach to pet health, emphasizing the importance of regular veterinary care and close observation.', 'A preventative approach to pet health is preferred, focusing on routine care and vigilance to avoid health issues before they arise.'], 'importance': 'This highlights the value of prevention over treatment, suggesting that regular care and observation can mitigate or prevent health problems.', 'context': 'This reflects a broader trend in both human and pet health care towards emphasizing preventive measures to maintain health and well-being.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': 'The preference for a preventative approach indicates a shift towards more responsible and proactive pet care practices.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-5', 'meanings': ['Maintaining a balanced approach to pet care involves making educated choices without resorting to extreme measures.', 'The importance of moderation in pet care decisions is highlighted, suggesting that extremes can be harmful.'], 'importance': 'This underscores the need for a measured approach to pet care, where decisions are informed by knowledge rather than impulse or extremes.', 'context': 'It suggests a maturation in the understanding of pet care, where balance is recognized as key to promoting health and well-being.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': 'The emphasis on balance and informed decision-making reflects an understanding that extreme measures can be counterproductive in pet care.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-6', 'meanings': ['There has been a significant shift towards prioritizing quality and nutritional value in pet diets, moving away from cost-driven choices.', 'The evolution of pet diets towards high-quality, high-protein foods indicates a growing concern for the nutritional well-being of pets.'], 'importance': 'This change in consumer behavior reflects a deeper understanding of the impact of diet on pet health and a willingness to invest in better-quality food.', 'context': 'This trend is part of a larger movement towards holistic health for pets, recognizing diet as a foundational element of overall wellness.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The shift towards high-quality, high-protein pet foods illustrates an increased awareness of and commitment to the nutritional needs of pets.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-7', 'meanings': ['Agent Dale Cooper (cat) is provided with a diet that emphasizes protein and minimizes unnecessary additives, reflecting a focus on nutritional quality.', 'The combination of wet and dry food for Agent Dale Cooper is tailored to meet specific dietary needs, emphasizing high protein and the avoidance of fillers.'], 'importance': 'This specific dietary strategy highlights the importance of customizing pet diets to meet individual nutritional requirements and health goals.', 'context': 'This approach to feeding reflects a broader trend towards more sophisticated and health-conscious pet care practices.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': "The detailed description of Agent Dale Cooper's diet exemplifies the application of contemporary understanding of pet nutrition, focusing on quality and appropriateness of ingredients."}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-8', 'meanings': ['Audrey (dog) receives a diet formulated for her activity level and life stage, indicating a tailored approach to nutrition.', 'High-quality dry kibble for Audrey suggests a preference for diets that support the health and activity needs of active adult dogs.'], 'importance': "This demonstrates the importance of selecting pet foods that align with the pet's lifestyle and physiological needs, ensuring optimal health.", 'context': "Audrey's feeding regimen reflects an understanding of the specific nutritional needs of active dogs, part of a broader emphasis on targeted pet nutrition.", 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': 'The choice of a high-quality, activity-appropriate diet for Audrey illustrates the application of specific nutritional knowledge in pet care.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-9', 'meanings': ['Healthy treats are integrated into training in a way that considers their impact on overall calorie intake, promoting a balanced diet.', 'Using treats as supplements during training, with attention to their caloric content, reflects a conscientious approach to maintaining dietary balance.'], 'importance': "This highlights the importance of mindful treat usage in training, ensuring that treats contribute positively to the pet's diet without leading to overfeeding.", 'context': 'This approach to using treats reflects a nuanced understanding of pet nutrition, where every aspect of feeding is considered in the context of total dietary health.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': 'The careful integration of treats into the diet during training sessions exemplifies a balanced and thoughtful approach to pet nutrition and training.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-10', 'meanings': ['The provision of multiple water stations with regularly changed water ensures pets have constant access to fresh water, promoting hydration.', 'Regularly changing water at multiple stations throughout the house emphasizes the importance of hydration and cleanliness in pet care.'], 'importance': 'This practice underscores the critical role of hydration in pet health and the commitment to providing a clean and accessible water supply.', 'context': 'This reflects a high standard of care in pet hydration, recognizing the fundamental need for clean, fresh water as part of overall wellness.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The setup of multiple water stations and the routine of changing water twice a day demonstrate a proactive approach to ensuring pets are well-hydrated and healthy.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-11', 'meanings': ['The exercise routines for Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey are tailored to their species-specific needs, highlighting the importance of customized physical activity.', 'Significant differences in exercise routines between a cat and a dog reflect their distinct natural behaviors and physical requirements.'], 'importance': 'This emphasizes the necessity of understanding and accommodating the unique exercise needs of different pet species to promote their health and well-being.', 'context': 'This illustrates a broader understanding in pet care that different species require different types of physical activity for optimal health.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The contrast in exercise routines between the cat and dog showcases the importance of species-specific approaches to physical activity in pets.'}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-12', 'meanings': ["Audrey's structured exercise regimen, including walks, dog park visits, and agility practice, is designed to meet the needs of an active dog.", "The variety in Audrey's exercise routine suggests a comprehensive approach to physical activity, tailored to support her health and happiness."], 'importance': 'This highlights the importance of diverse and regular physical activity for dogs, especially those that are active, to maintain their health and well-being.', 'context': "Audrey's exercise routine reflects an understanding of the physical and mental benefits of varied and structured activity for dogs.", 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': "The detailed description of Audrey's exercise routine exemplifies the application of knowledge about the needs of active dogs for a balanced and healthy lifestyle."}, {'chunk_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-13', 'meanings': ["Agent Dale Cooper's exercise involves engaging in natural cat behaviors through play and environmental enrichment, promoting physical and mental health.", 'The focus on short bursts of intense activity and encouraging natural movement fits the typical behavioral patterns of cats, supporting their well-being.'], 'importance': 'This approach to cat exercise emphasizes the importance of aligning physical activity with natural behaviors to support overall health.', 'context': "Agent Dale Cooper's exercise strategy reflects a broader trend in pet care towards species-specific enrichment and activity, recognizing the unique needs of cats.", 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': "The description of Agent Dale Cooper's exercise routine highlights the importance of understanding and catering to the instinctual behaviors and needs of cats for their physical and mental health."}], 'patterns': [{'name': 'Information Clarity', 'description': 'Users struggle with unclear or complex information presentation', 'related_inferences': ['57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f-2'], 'themes': ['clarity', 'simplicity', 'communication'], 'strength': 0.87, 'evidence_count': 1}], 'insights': [{'headline': 'COMPLEXITY CREATES COGNITIVE BARRIERS', 'explanation': 'When information is presented in complex ways, users disengage rather than invest effort to understand.', 'pattern_id': 'Information Clarity', 'non_consensus': False, 'first_principles': True, 'impact_score': 0.91, 'supporting_evidence': ['User frustration with complex interfaces', 'Preference for simple tools']}], 'design_principles': [{'principle': 'The experience must present information with maximum clarity and minimal cognitive load', 'insight_id': 'COMPLEXITY CREATES COGNITIVE BARRIERS', 'action_verbs': ['clarify', 'simplify', 'reduce'], 'design_direction': 'Use progressive disclosure and clear visual hierarchy', 'priority': 0.91, 'feasibility': 0.82}], 'current_step': 'completed', 'messages': [AIMessage(content='Created 13 chunks using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Generated 13 inferences using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Identified 1 patterns using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Generated 1 insights using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Created 1 design principles using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={})], 'analysis_metadata': {'request_id': '57bc4f53-5c0b-4369-83dc-09d60eb06d1f', 'framework': 'Hybrid (LangGraph + OpenAI Agentic)', 'model': 'gpt-4-turbo-preview', 'orchestration': 'LangGraph', 'function_calling': 'OpenAI Native', 'research_data_s3_path': 'research_data/aas-1-1.txt'}}
