': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_b1c2c839', 'content': 'Beyond structured exercise, Audrey gets mental stimulation through training sessions. We do about 10-15 minutes of training every evening. Sometimes it\'s basic obedience reinforcement, sometimes we\'re learning new tricks. Right now, we\'re working on "tidy up," where she puts her toys back in the toy basket. She\'s getting pretty good at it, though she sometimes tries to cheat by just dropping them near the basket rather than in it.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_33bc8999', 'content': 'Agent Dale Cooper\'s exercise needs are totally different. Cats need short bursts of intense activity rather than sustained exercise. I do two dedicated play sessions with him daily - one in the morning after breakfast and one in the evening before bed. Each session is about 15-20 minutes, or until he starts panting or loses interest. I use different toys to simulate hunting behaviors - feather wands for bird-like prey, laser pointers for quick movement (though I always end with a physical toy so he can actually "catch" something), and these little fake mice that he likes to carry around.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_40d42048', 'content': 'The interesting thing about Agent Dale Cooper is that he\'s most active at dawn and dusk - classic cat behavior. So around 5 AM, I often hear him racing around upstairs, doing what I call his "morning zoomies." He runs from room to room, jumps on and off furniture, and generally acts like he\'s possessed for about 10 minutes. Then he\'s done and goes back to sleep. He does the same thing around 9 PM.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_cf56e682', 'content': "I've also set up the house to encourage natural movement for him. I have cat trees in three different rooms, shelves mounted on the walls to create climbing paths, and window perches where he can watch birds. He probably climbs up and down his various perches 20-30 times a day. I've actually watched him sometimes, and he has favorite routes through the house that involve jumping from surface to surface without touching the floor - like the floor is lava or something.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_3875999e', 'content': "One challenge is that Agent Dale Cooper is an indoor-only cat, so I have to be creative about exercise. I've trained him to walk on a harness and leash, and we go out in the backyard sometimes, but he's not really into it. He mostly just sits and eats grass and glares at me for subjecting him to the indignity of a harness. But the indoor play sessions seem to be enough for him - he maintains a healthy weight and the vet says his muscle tone is good.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-1', 'content': 'Pet wellness is about the whole picture, not just preventing sickness but ensuring pets thrive and are happy.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'holistic approach']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-2', 'content': 'Physical health and mental/emotional wellbeing are both important aspects of pet wellness.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'physical health', 'mental health']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-3', 'content': 'Cats and dogs have different needs for mental stimulation and physical activity.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cats vs dogs', 'activity needs']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-4', 'content': 'Alex Morrison prefers a preventative approach to pet health, focusing on regular vet visits and daily observation.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['preventative care', 'pet health']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-5', 'content': 'Balance in pet care is important, avoiding extremes and making informed decisions.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['balanced care', 'informed decisions']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-6', 'content': 'Diet for pets has evolved from basic grocery store food to high-quality, researched options.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['pet diet', 'nutrition']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-7', 'content': "Agent Dale Cooper's diet includes a mix of high-quality wet and dry food, with attention to protein content and variety.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cat diet', 'high-quality food']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-8', 'content': "Audrey's diet is formulated for active adult dogs, with glucosamine for joint health and calorie-counted treats.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['dog diet', 'active dogs']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-9', 'content': 'Water intake is closely monitored for both pets, with multiple water stations and specific preferences addressed.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['hydration', 'water intake']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-10', 'content': "Exercise routines are tailored to each pet's species and individual needs, with structured activities and mental sti