2025-11-02 22:50:05,226 - hybrid_agentic_analysis - INFO - combined result: {'tracker': <dynamodb_tracker.DynamoDBTracker object at 0x10c453170>, 'input_config': InputConfig(project_name='Debug Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices'), 'project_config': ProjectConfig(project_name='Debug Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices', project_id='4fbd253f-9366-41c5-8de8-daa65df18de3', result_path='projects/4fbd253f-9366-41c5-8de8-daa65df18de3'), 'project_result': HybridAnalysisResponse(request_id='0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198', status='completed', implementation='hybrid', timestamp='2025-11-02T17:15:44.300521+00:00', chunks=[{'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_573d0358', 'content': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_3ecc6f05', 'content': 'Date: March 15, 2024', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_f8231ac2', 'content': 'Interviewer: Research Team Member', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_d0ce11be', 'content': 'Interviewee: Alex Morrison (Pet Parent)', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_fa30c144', 'content': 'Duration: 45 minutes', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_aec001cb', 'content': 'Pets: Agent Dale Cooper (Cat, 6 years old) and Audrey Horne (Dog - Golden Retriever, 4 years old)', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_66327935', 'content': 'Question 1: Can you tell me about your overall approach to keeping Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey Horne healthy? What does pet wellness mean to you?', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_66553476', 'content': "Response: Oh, that's such a big question to start with! For me, pet wellness is really about looking at the whole picture, you know? It's not just about making sure they're not sick - it's about them thriving and being happy. With Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey, I think about it in layers. There's the physical health aspect, obviously - making sure they're at a good weight, their coats are shiny, they're active. But there's also the mental and emotional side that I think people sometimes overlook.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_44f81509', 'content': "Agent Dale Cooper, being a cat, he needs different things than Audrey does. He needs mental stimulation through play, places to climb and perch, windows to look out of. He's very particular about his environment being just right. Audrey, on the other hand, she needs that social interaction, the physical exercise, the training that keeps her mind engaged.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_ac274da1', 'content': "I guess my overall approach is preventative rather than reactive. I'd rather invest time and energy into keeping them healthy than dealing with problems after they arise. That means regular vet visits, yes, but also daily observation. I know their normal behaviors so well that I can tell immediately if something's off. Like last month, Agent Dale Cooper was just sitting differently - nothing dramatic, but I could tell his posture was off. Turned out he had a minor muscle strain from jumping weird off the cat tree.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_91417ea5', 'content': "I also believe in balance. I'm not one of those pet parents who goes to extremes - I don't cook elaborate meals from scratch every day or anything like that. But I do research everything I give them, every toy I buy, every change I make to their routine. It's about making informed decisions that work for our lifestyle while prioritizing their wellbeing.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_48c2c004', 'content': "Question 2: Let's talk about diet specifically. What do you feed Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey, and how did you decide on their current feeding routines?", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_c9b94c53', 'content': "Response: Diet has been quite a journey for us, actually. When I first got Agent Dale Cooper five years ago, I just bought whatever cat food was on sale at the grocery store. I didn't know any better. But then he started having some digestive issues - nothing serious, but enough that the vet suggested I look into higher quality food. That sent me down this whole rabbit hole of pet nutrition research.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_cd1a2fca', 'content': "For Agent Dale Cooper now, I feed him a combination of high-quality wet and dry food. In the morning, he gets about 3 ounces of wet food - I rotate between three different brands to give him variety. Right now, I'm using brands that focus on high protein content with no fillers or by-products. The first ingredient is always actual meat, not meal or by-product. He gets salmon-based food twice a week because it's good for his coat, and chicken or turkey the other days. I tried duck once, but he looked at me like I'd personally offended him and refused to eat it for two days.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_26ba2a81', 'content': "Throughout the day, he has access to dry food, but I measure it out - about 1/4 cup total. I learned the hard way that free-feeding without limits led to him gaining two pounds in three months. The vet wasn't happy about that. His dry food is a dental health formula because cats are prone to dental issues, and honestly, trying to brush Agent Dale Cooper's teeth is like trying to negotiate with a tiny, furry tornado.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_46ae24d6', 'content': "Audrey's diet is different because she's much more active and, being a Golden Retriever, she has different nutritional needs. She gets fed twice a day - morning and evening. I give her about 1.5 cups of high-quality dry kibble each meal, so 3 cups total per day. Her food is specifically formulated for active adult dogs, with glucosamine for joint health since Goldens can have hip issues later in life.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_eef97d1a', 'content': "I supplement Audrey's diet with healthy treats during training - things like small pieces of carrot, green beans, or these little freeze-dried liver treats that she goes absolutely crazy for. But I count those calories as part of her daily intake. I learned to do that after she gained five pounds one summer when I was doing a lot of training with her and didn't account for all those treats.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_4438bd4a', 'content': "Oh, and water! I'm obsessive about water. They both have multiple water stations around the house, and I change the water twice a day. Agent Dale Cooper has this fancy ceramic fountain because cats prefer moving water, apparently. Audrey just has regular bowls, but I have one inside and one outside because she's always running in and out.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_c948eca4', 'content': "The timing of meals is important too. Agent Dale Cooper gets his wet food at 7 AM and 6 PM like clockwork. If I'm even five minutes late, he sits by his bowl and gives me this look of utter betrayal. Audrey eats at 7:30 AM and 5:30 PM. I feed them at slightly different times to avoid any food competition issues, even though they respect each other's bowls pretty well.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_d360df3f', 'content': 'Question 3: How do you handle exercise and physical activity for each of your pets? What does a typical day look like?', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_256f16e8', 'content': 'Response: Exercise routines are completely different for each of them, as you can imagine! Audrey is my marathon runner, and Agent Dale Cooper is more of a sprinter who believes in strategic energy conservation.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_e84d0319', 'content': "Let me start with Audrey because her routine is more structured. We begin every single day with a morning walk, rain or shine. I wake up at 6 AM, and by 6:30, we're out the door. The morning walk is usually about 45 minutes to an hour, depending on the weather and my schedule. We have three different routes we rotate through to keep things interesting for her. One goes through the park where she can sniff all the good smells, another goes past the lake where she sometimes gets to swim in summer, and the third is more of an urban route where we practice her leash manners around distractions.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_687245fb', 'content': "After work, around 5 PM, before dinner, we do another activity. Three days a week, this is another walk, usually 30 minutes. But twice a week, we go to the dog park instead, where she can really run and play with other dogs for about an hour. Weekends are when we do our big adventures - hiking trails, beach trips if the weather's nice, or sometimes agility practice in the backyard. I set up some basic agility equipment - nothing fancy, just some jumps and weave poles - and she loves it.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_b1c2c839', 'content': 'Beyond structured exercise, Audrey gets mental stimulation through training sessions. We do about 10-15 minutes of training every evening. Sometimes it\'s basic obedience reinforcement, sometimes we\'re learning new tricks. Right now, we\'re working on "tidy up," where she puts her toys back in the toy basket. She\'s getting pretty good at it, though she sometimes tries to cheat by just dropping them near the basket rather than in it.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_33bc8999', 'content': 'Agent Dale Cooper\'s exercise needs are totally different. Cats need short bursts of intense activity rather than sustained exercise. I do two dedicated play sessions with him daily - one in the morning after breakfast and one in the evening before bed. Each session is about 15-20 minutes, or until he starts panting or loses interest. I use different toys to simulate hunting behaviors - feather wands for bird-like prey, laser pointers for quick movement (though I always end with a physical toy so he can actually "catch" something), and these little fake mice that he likes to carry around.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_40d42048', 'content': 'The interesting thing about Agent Dale Cooper is that he\'s most active at dawn and dusk - classic cat behavior. So around 5 AM, I often hear him racing around upstairs, doing what I call his "morning zoomies." He runs from room to room, jumps on and off furniture, and generally acts like he\'s possessed for about 10 minutes. Then he\'s done and goes back to sleep. He does the same thing around 9 PM.', 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_cf56e682', 'content': "I've also set up the house to encourage natural movement for him. I have cat trees in three different rooms, shelves mounted on the walls to create climbing paths, and window perches where he can watch birds. He probably climbs up and down his various perches 20-30 times a day. I've actually watched him sometimes, and he has favorite routes through the house that involve jumping from surface to surface without touching the floor - like the floor is lava or something.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_3875999e', 'content': "One challenge is that Agent Dale Cooper is an indoor-only cat, so I have to be creative about exercise. I've trained him to walk on a harness and leash, and we go out in the backyard sometimes, but he's not really into it. He mostly just sits and eats grass and glares at me for subjecting him to the indignity of a harness. But the indoor play sessions seem to be enough for him - he maintains a healthy weight and the vet says his muscle tone is good.", 'source': 'research_data', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.85, 'tags': ['general']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-1', 'content': 'Pet wellness is about the whole picture, not just preventing sickness but ensuring pets thrive and are happy.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'holistic approach']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-2', 'content': 'Physical health and mental/emotional wellbeing are both important aspects of pet wellness.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'physical health', 'mental health']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-3', 'content': 'Cats and dogs have different needs for mental stimulation and physical activity.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cats vs dogs', 'activity needs']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-4', 'content': 'Alex Morrison prefers a preventative approach to pet health, focusing on regular vet visits and daily observation.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['preventative care', 'pet health']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-5', 'content': 'Balance in pet care is important, avoiding extremes and making informed decisions.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['balanced care', 'informed decisions']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-6', 'content': 'Diet for pets has evolved from basic grocery store food to high-quality, researched options.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['pet diet', 'nutrition']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-7', 'content': "Agent Dale Cooper's diet includes a mix of high-quality wet and dry food, with attention to protein content and variety.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cat diet', 'high-quality food']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-8', 'content': "Audrey's diet is formulated for active adult dogs, with glucosamine for joint health and calorie-counted treats.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['dog diet', 'active dogs']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-9', 'content': 'Water intake is closely monitored for both pets, with multiple water stations and specific preferences addressed.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['hydration', 'water intake']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-10', 'content': "Exercise routines are tailored to each pet's species and individual needs, with structured activities and mental stimulation.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['exercise routine', 'mental stimulation']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-11', 'content': "Audrey's exercise includes daily walks, dog park visits, and agility practice, alongside training sessions for mental stimulation.", 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['dog exercise', 'mental stimulation']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-12', 'content': 'Agent Dale Cooper engages in short bursts of intense activity, with play sessions designed to simulate hunting behaviors.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cat exercise', 'play sessions']}, {'id': '0d1b091a-c5fe-4af6-9ea2-f27e8c513198-13', 'content': 'The home environment is set up to encourage natural movement for Agent Dale Cooper, with cat trees, shelves, and window perches.', 'source': 'Interview with Alex Morrison', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['home setup', 'natural movement']}], inferences=[{'chunk_id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_573d0358', 'meanings': ['Users have specific needs and preferences'], 'importance': 'Reveals user behavior patterns and needs', 'context': 'Indicates fundamental user preferences', 'confidence': 0.88, 'reasoning': 'Based on user feedback patterns'}, {'chunk_id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_3ecc6f05', 'meanings': ['Users have specific needs and preferences'], 'importance': 'Reveals user behavior patterns and needs', 'context': 'Indicates fundamental user preferences', 'confidence': 0.88, 'reasoning': 'Based on user feedback patterns'}, {'chunk_id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_f8231ac2', 'meanings': ['Users have specific needs and preferences'], 'importance': 'Reveals user behavior patterns and needs', 'context': 'Indicates fundamental user preferences', 'confidence': 0.88, 'reasoning': 'Based on user feedback patterns'}, {'chunk_id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_d0ce11be', 'meanings': ['Users have specific needs and preferences'], 'importance': 'Reveals user behavior patterns and needs', 'context': 'Indicates fundamental user preferences', 'confidence': 0.88, 'reasoning': 'Based on user feedback patterns'}, {'chunk_id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_fa30c144', 'meanings': ['Users have specific needs and preferences'], 'importance': 'Reveals user behavior patterns and needs', 'context': 'Indicates fundamental user preferences', 'confidence': 0.88, 'reasoning': 'Based on user feedback patterns'}, {'chunk_id': '2612571f-98b6-45e0-af06-7d8884044847-chunk_aec001cb', 'meanings': ['Users have specific needs and preferences'], 'importance': 'Reveals user behavior patterns and needs', 'context': 'Indicates fundament