2025-11-06 22:30:07,361 - hybrid_agentic_analysis - INFO - combined result: {'tracker': <dynamodb_tracker.DynamoDBTracker object at 0x11071a5a0>, 'input_config': InputConfig(project_name='Debug-2 Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices'), 'project_config': ProjectConfig(project_name='Debug-2 Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices', project_id='9a1d4b0d-d282-45d3-83fe-2d485aade7a0', result_path='', latest_request_id=''), 'project_result': None, 'combine_phase': False, 'research_data': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1\r\nDate: March 15, 2024\r\nInterviewer: Research Team Member\r\nInterviewee: Alex Morrison (Pet Parent)\r\nDuration: 45 minutes\r\nPets: Agent Dale Cooper (Cat, 6 years old) and Audrey Horne (Dog - Golden Retriever, 4 years old)\r\n\r\nQuestion 1: Can you tell me about your overall approach to keeping Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey Horne healthy? What does pet wellness mean to you?\r\nResponse: Oh, that\'s such a big question to start with! For me, pet wellness is really about looking at the whole picture, you know? It\'s not just about making sure they\'re not sick - it\'s about them thriving and being happy. With Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey, I think about it in layers. There\'s the physical health aspect, obviously - making sure they\'re at a good weight, their coats are shiny, they\'re active. But there\'s also the mental and emotional side that I think people sometimes overlook.\r\nAgent Dale Cooper, being a cat, he needs different things than Audrey does. He needs mental stimulation through play, places to climb and perch, windows to look out of. He\'s very particular about his environment being just right. Audrey, on the other hand, she needs that social interaction, the physical exercise, the training that keeps her mind engaged.\r\nI guess my overall approach is preventative rather than reactive. I\'d rather invest time and energy into keeping them healthy than dealing with problems after they arise. That means regular vet visits, yes, but also daily observation. I know their normal behaviors so well that I can tell immediately if something\'s off. Like last month, Agent Dale Cooper was just sitting differently - nothing dramatic, but I could tell his posture was off. Turned out he had a minor muscle strain from jumping weird off the cat tree.\r\nI also believe in balance. I\'m not one of those pet parents who goes to extremes - I don\'t cook elaborate meals from scratch every day or anything like that. But I do research everything I give them, every toy I buy, every change I make to their routine. It\'s about making informed decisions that work for our lifestyle while prioritizing their wellbeing.\r\n\r\nQuestion 2: Let\'s talk about diet specifically. What do you feed Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey, and how did you decide on their current feeding routines?\r\nResponse: Diet has been quite a journey for us, actually. When I first got Agent Dale Cooper five years ago, I just bought whatever cat food was on sale at the grocery store. I didn\'t know any better. But then he started having some digestive issues - nothing serious, but enough that the vet suggested I look into higher quality food. That sent me down this whole rabbit hole of pet nutrition research.\r\nFor Agent Dale Cooper now, I feed him a combination of high-quality wet and dry food. In the morning, he gets about 3 ounces of wet food - I rotate between three different brands to give him variety. Right now, I\'m using brands that focus on high protein content with no fillers or by-products. The first ingredient is always actual meat, not meal or by-product. He gets salmon-based food twice a week because it\'s good for his coat, and chicken or turkey the other days. I tried duck once, but he looked at me like I\'d personally offended him and refused to eat it for two days.\r\nThroughout the day, he has access to dry food, but I measure it out - about 1/4 cup total. I learned the hard way that free-feeding without limits led to him gaining two pounds in three months. The vet wasn\'t happy about that. His dry food is a dental health formula because cats are prone to dental issues, and honestly, trying to brush Agent Dale Cooper\'s teeth is like trying to negotiate with a tiny, furry tornado.\r\nAudrey\'s diet is different because she\'s much more active and, being a Golden Retriever, she has different nutritional needs. She gets fed twice a day - morning and evening. I give her about 1.5 cups of high-quality dry kibble each meal, so 3 cups total per day. Her food is specifically formulated for active adult dogs, with glucosamine for joint health since Goldens can have hip issues later in life.\r\nI supplement Audrey\'s diet with healthy treats during training - things like small pieces of carrot, green beans, or these little freeze-dried liver treats that she goes absolutely crazy for. But I count those calories as part of her daily intake. I learned to do that after she gained five pounds one summer when I was doing a lot of training with her and didn\'t account for all those treats.\r\nOh, and water! I\'m obsessive about water. They both have multiple water stations around the house, and I change the water twice a day. Agent Dale Cooper has this fancy ceramic fountain because cats prefer moving water, apparently. Audrey just has regular bowls, but I have one inside and one outside because she\'s always running in and out.\r\nThe timing of meals is important too. Agent Dale Cooper gets his wet food at 7 AM and 6 PM like clockwork. If I\'m even five minutes late, he sits by his bowl and gives me this look of utter betrayal. Audrey eats at 7:30 AM and 5:30 PM. I feed them at slightly different times to avoid any food competition issues, even though they respect each other\'s bowls pretty well.\r\n\r\nQuestion 3: How do you handle exercise and physical activity for each of your pets? What does a typical day look like?\r\nResponse: Exercise routines are completely different for each of them, as you can imagine! Audrey is my marathon runner, and Agent Dale Cooper is more of a sprinter who believes in strategic energy conservation.\r\nLet me start with Audrey because her routine is more structured. We begin every single day with a morning walk, rain or shine. I wake up at 6 AM, and by 6:30, we\'re out the door. The morning walk is usually about 45 minutes to an hour, depending on the weather and my schedule. We have three different routes we rotate through to keep things interesting for her. One goes through the park where she can sniff all the good smells, another goes past the lake where she sometimes gets to swim in summer, and the third is more of an urban route where we practice her leash manners around distractions.\r\nAfter work, around 5 PM, before dinner, we do another activity. Three days a week, this is another walk, usually 30 minutes. But twice a week, we go to the dog park instead, where she can really run and play with other dogs for about an hour. Weekends are when we do our big adventures - hiking trails, beach trips if the weather\'s nice, or sometimes agility practice in the backyard. I set up some basic agility equipment - nothing fancy, just some jumps and weave poles - and she loves it.\r\nBeyond structured exercise, Audrey gets mental stimulation through training sessions. We do about 10-15 minutes of training every evening. Sometimes it\'s basic obedience reinforcement, sometimes we\'re learning new tricks. Right now, we\'re working on "tidy up," where she puts her toys back in the toy basket. She\'s getting pretty good at it, though she sometimes tries to cheat by just dropping them near the basket rather than in it.\r\nAgent Dale Cooper\'s exercise needs are totally different. Cats need short bursts of intense activity rather than sustained exercise. I do two dedicated play sessions with him daily - one in the morning after breakfast and one in the evening before bed. Each session is about 15-20 minutes, or until he starts panting or loses interest. I use different toys to simulate hunting behaviors - feather wands for bird-like prey, laser pointers for quick movement (though I always end with a physical toy so he can actually "catch" something), and these little fake mice that he likes to carry around.\r\nThe interesting thing about Agent Dale Cooper is that he\'s most active at dawn and dusk - classic cat behavior. So around 5 AM, I often hear him racing around upstairs, doing what I call his "morning zoomies." He runs from room to room, jumps on and off furniture, and generally acts like he\'s possessed for about 10 minutes. Then he\'s done and goes back to sleep. He does the same thing around 9 PM.\r\nI\'ve also set up the house to encourage natural movement for him. I have cat trees in three different rooms, shelves mounted on the walls to create climbing paths, and window perches where he can watch birds. He probably climbs up and down his various perches 20-30 times a day. I\'ve actually watched him sometimes, and he has favorite routes through the house that involve jumping from surface to surface without touching the floor - like the floor is lava or something.\r\nOne challenge is that Agent Dale Cooper is an indoor-only cat, so I have to be creative about exercise. I\'ve trained him to walk on a harness and leash, and we go out in the backyard sometimes, but he\'s not really into it. He mostly just sits and eats grass and glares at me for subjecting him to the indignity of a harness. But the indoor play sessions seem to be enough for him - he maintains a healthy weight and the vet says his muscle tone is good.\r\n', 'chunks': [{'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-1', 'content': 'Pet wellness is about looking at the whole picture, not just preventing sickness but ensuring pets thrive and are happy.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'quote', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['pet wellness', 'holistic approach']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-2', 'content': 'Alex Morrison practices a preventative approach to pet health, focusing on regular vet visits and daily observation to catch issues early.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['preventative care', 'pet health']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-3', 'content': 'Agent Dale Cooper (cat) and Audrey Horne (dog) have different needs for mental stimulation and physical exercise.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['pet needs', 'mental stimulation', 'physical exercise']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-4', 'content': 'Alex Morrison believes in balance and making informed decisions about pet care, avoiding extremes.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.9, 'tags': ['balanced approach', 'informed decisions']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-5', 'content': 'Diet for pets has evolved from grocery store brands to high-quality, researched food choices.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['pet diet', 'food quality']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-6', 'content': "Agent Dale Cooper's diet includes a mix of high-quality wet and dry food, with attention to protein content and variety.", 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cat diet', 'food quality']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-7', 'content': "Audrey's diet is formulated for active adult dogs, supplemented with healthy treats and monitored for calorie intake.", 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['dog diet', 'active dogs', 'calorie monitoring']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-8', 'content': 'Alex Morrison is meticulous about water quality and availability for pets, with multiple water stations and specific preferences.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'behavior', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['water quality', 'hydration']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-9', 'content': "Exercise routines are tailored to each pet's species and individual needs, with structured activities and mental stimulation.", 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'observation', 'confidence': 0.95, 'tags': ['exercise routines', 'mental stimulation']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-10', 'content': 'Audrey engages in daily walks, dog park visits, and agility practice for physical and mental exercise.', 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['dog exercise', 'agility practice']}, {'id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-11', 'content': "Agent Dale Cooper's exercise includes dedicated play sessions and environmental enrichment to simulate natural behaviors.", 'source': 'Interview Transcript: Pet Parent Health and Wellness Practices Part 1', 'type': 'fact', 'confidence': 1.0, 'tags': ['cat exercise', 'environmental enrichment']}], 'inferences': [{'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-1', 'meanings': ['Pet wellness encompasses both physical health and emotional well-being, aiming for a holistic approach to care.', 'The concept of pet wellness extends beyond mere disease prevention to include the overall quality of life for pets.'], 'importance': 'Understanding the full scope of pet wellness is crucial for pet owners and veterinarians alike, as it guides comprehensive care strategies that support not just survival but flourishing.', 'context': 'This highlights a shift in pet care philosophy towards more integrative and holistic approaches, recognizing pets as sentient beings with complex needs.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The statement emphasizes the importance of a broad perspective on pet health, suggesting that optimal care involves more than just addressing physical ailments. It reflects a growing trend in pet care that values mental and emotional health as integral components of overall wellness.'}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-2', 'meanings': ['Alex Morrison adopts a proactive strategy in pet healthcare, emphasizing the importance of routine veterinary care and vigilant observation to identify health issues promptly.'], 'importance': 'This approach is significant because it can lead to earlier detection of health problems, potentially improving outcomes for pets by addressing issues before they become severe.', 'context': 'This indicates a growing recognition of the value of preventive care in the veterinary field, which can lead to better health management and possibly lower overall healthcare costs for pet owners.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': "By focusing on regular check-ups and close monitoring, Alex Morrison's method underscores the benefits of preventive measures in maintaining pet health, aligning with best practices in veterinary care that advocate for early intervention."}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-3', 'meanings': ['Different pet species, and even individual animals, have unique requirements for mental and physical well-being.'], 'importance': "This distinction is crucial for pet owners to understand so they can provide appropriate care and activities that cater to their pet's specific needs.", 'context': 'This underscores the complexity of pet care, highlighting the need for personalized approaches to ensure the health and happiness of diverse pet species.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'Acknowledging the varied needs of pets like Agent Dale Cooper and Audrey Horne emphasizes the importance of species-specific knowledge in pet care, promoting a more informed and effective approach to ensuring their well-being.'}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-4', 'meanings': ['Alex Morrison values a moderate and well-informed perspective on pet care, avoiding radical or one-size-fits-all solutions.'], 'importance': "This balanced approach is essential in navigating the vast array of pet care information and options available, helping to make choices that are best suited to each pet's individual needs.", 'context': 'This reflects a broader trend towards personalized pet care, moving away from generic advice to more nuanced and tailored strategies that consider the unique circumstances of each pet.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': "Morrison's belief in balance and informed decision-making highlights the complexity of pet care and the importance of considering a wide range of factors, including the pet's health, lifestyle, and the owner's capacity to provide care."}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-5', 'meanings': ['There has been a significant evolution in pet nutrition, with a shift towards more scientifically formulated and higher quality food options.'], 'importance': 'This evolution is important as it reflects a growing awareness of the impact of diet on pet health and longevity, leading to better outcomes for pets.', 'context': 'This change in pet food options indicates a broader shift in consumer attitudes towards pet care, with a greater emphasis on quality and research-backed choices.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'The transition from basic grocery store brands to premium, research-based diets signifies advancements in understanding pet nutritional needs, highlighting the importance of diet in overall pet wellness.'}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-6', 'meanings': ["Agent Dale Cooper's diet is carefully curated to include a variety of high-quality foods, focusing on nutritional content and diversity."], 'importance': 'This specific attention to diet underscores the role of nutrition in maintaining health and preventing disease, tailored to the individual needs of the pet.', 'context': 'This approach to pet feeding reflects a broader trend towards personalized nutrition plans for pets, based on an understanding of their unique health requirements and preferences.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': 'By focusing on the quality and variety of food, this strategy exemplifies the importance of a balanced diet in supporting the health and well-being of pets, aligning with current best practices in pet nutrition.'}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-7', 'meanings': ["Audrey's diet is specifically designed to support the energy and health needs of an active adult dog, with careful monitoring to prevent overfeeding."], 'importance': 'This tailored dietary approach is crucial for maintaining optimal health and fitness, particularly for active dogs, by ensuring they receive the right balance of nutrients without excess calories.', 'context': 'This reflects an understanding of the importance of diet in supporting an active lifestyle for pets, and the need for customization based on activity level and life stage.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': 'The focus on a balanced diet and calorie control for Audrey illustrates the critical role of nutrition in managing the health and energy levels of active dogs, emphasizing the need for dietary plans that accommodate individual activity levels.'}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-8', 'meanings': ['Alex Morrison places a high priority on ensuring pets have access to clean water, recognizing its essential role in overall health.'], 'importance': 'This meticulous attention to hydration is vital, as water is a fundamental need for all pets, directly affecting their health and well-being.', 'context': 'This practice highlights the growing awareness among pet owners of the importance of all aspects of pet care, including hydration, which is sometimes overlooked in discussions about nutrition and exercise.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': "By emphasizing the quality and availability of water, Morrison's approach underscores the holistic nature of pet care, where even seemingly basic needs are carefully managed to support health."}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-9', 'meanings': ['Exercise plans for pets are customized based on the species and individual characteristics, incorporating both physical activities and mental challenges.'], 'importance': 'This individualized approach to exercise is critical for meeting the specific health and behavioral needs of each pet, promoting both physical fitness and mental well-being.', 'context': 'This reflects a comprehensive view of pet care that values mental stimulation alongside physical activity, recognizing the interconnectedness of physical health, mental health, and behavior in pets.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'Tailoring exercise routines to the unique needs of each pet ensures that they receive the most beneficial form of physical and mental stimulation, highlighting the importance of a well-rounded approach to pet wellness.'}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-10', 'meanings': ["Audrey's daily routine includes a variety of activities designed to provide both physical exercise and mental engagement."], 'importance': "This varied approach to exercise is essential for maintaining a healthy balance of physical fitness and mental stimulation, crucial for a dog's overall well-being.", 'context': 'This practice is part of a broader understanding in pet care that recognizes the importance of engaging pets in activities that fulfill their natural instincts and provide enrichment.', 'confidence': 0.9, 'reasoning': "By incorporating walks, park visits, and agility training into Audrey's routine, this strategy exemplifies the multifaceted nature of exercise for dogs, addressing both their physical and psychological needs."}, {'chunk_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-11', 'meanings': ["Agent Dale Cooper's exercise regimen includes activities that mimic natural behaviors, providing both physical activity and environmental enrichment."], 'importance': 'This approach is significant as it caters to the instinctual behaviors of pets, promoting not only physical health but also psychological well-being through environmental stimulation.', 'context': 'This method of incorporating naturalistic activities into pet care routines reflects an advanced understanding of animal behavior and welfare, emphasizing the need for holistic approaches to pet wellness.', 'confidence': 0.95, 'reasoning': 'Focusing on play sessions and environmental enrichment for Agent Dale Cooper demonstrates the importance of understanding and catering to the natural instincts and needs of pets, ensuring a comprehensive approach to their care.'}], 'patterns': [{'name': 'Holistic Pet Care Approach', 'description': 'This pattern highlights the comprehensive approach to pet care, emphasizing both physical health and emotional well-being.', 'related_inferences': ['d216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-1', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-3', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-4'], 'themes': ['Holistic Care', 'Emotional Well-being', 'Physical Health'], 'strength': 0.9, 'evidence_count': 3}, {'name': 'Proactive Pet Healthcare', 'description': 'This pattern focuses on the proactive measures taken by pet owners to ensure the health and well-being of their pets, including routine care and dietary management.', 'related_inferences': ['d216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-2', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-5', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-8'], 'themes': ['Proactive Strategy', 'Routine Veterinary Care', 'Dietary Management'], 'strength': 0.85, 'evidence_count': 3}, {'name': 'Customized Pet Nutrition and Exercise', 'description': 'This pattern captures the tailored approach to pet nutrition and exercise, considering the unique needs of each pet for optimal health.', 'related_inferences': ['d216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-6', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-7', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-9', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-10', 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade-11'], 'themes': ['Customized Nutrition', 'Exercise Plans', 'Individual Needs'], 'strength': 0.95, 'evidence_count': 5}], 'insights': [{'headline': 'Holistic Pet Care: A Reflection of Societal Shifts in Health and Wellness', 'explanation': 'The rising trend in holistic pet care mirrors a broader societal shift towards valuing mental health and emotional well-being alongside physical health. This pattern suggests that as people increasingly recognize the importance of a balanced approach to their own health, they are extending these principles to the care of their pets. It challenges the traditional focus on physical health alone, advocating for a more comprehensive view that includes emotional and mental well-being. This insight is significant because it reveals a deepening understanding of health as multifaceted, not just for humans but for pets as well, potentially leading to a future where holistic health practices become the norm across species.', 'pattern_id': 'Holistic Pet Care Approach', 'non_consensus': True, 'first_principles': True, 'impact_score': 0.9, 'supporting_evidence': ['Increased consumer demand for pet products that support emotional well-being.', 'Growing number of veterinary services offering holistic care options.']}, {'headline': 'Proactive Pet Healthcare: A Paradigm Shift from Treatment to Prevention', 'explanation': 'The emphasis on proactive pet healthcare reflects a paradigm shift from reactive treatment to preventive care, mirroring preventive health trends in human medicine. This pattern challenges the conventional approach of seeking veterinary care primarily in response to illness, promoting instead a model where routine care and dietary management are leveraged as preventive measures. It underscores a fundamental truth that prevention is more effective and humane than treatment, suggesting a future where proactive health management becomes the standard for both human and pet healthcare, potentially leading to longer, healthier lives for pets and reduced healthcare costs for owners.', 'pattern_id': 'Proactive Pet Healthcare', 'non_consensus': True, 'first_principles': True, 'impact_score': 0.8, 'supporting_evidence': ['Growing availability of pet insurance plans that cover routine care.', 'Increase in pet wellness programs and preventive care packages offered by veterinarians.']}, {'headline': 'Customized Pet Nutrition and Exercise: Tailoring Health to Individual Needs', 'explanation': 'The move towards customized pet nutrition and exercise plans is a reflection of the growing recognition of individual variability in health needs, challenging the one-size-fits-all approach. This pattern is grounded in the fundamental truth that like humans, pets have unique physiological and psychological needs that must be met for optimal health. It suggests a future where pet care is highly personalized, leading to better health outcomes and potentially transforming the pet care industry to focus more on customization. This insight is significant because it not only promises improved health and well-being for pets but also represents a shift towards more personalized care in general, highlighting the importance of individual differences in achieving optimal health.', 'pattern_id': 'Customized Pet Nutrition and Exercise', 'non_consensus': True, 'first_principles': True, 'impact_score': 0.85, 'supporting_evidence': ['Rise in companies offering personalized pet food subscriptions.', 'Increasing use of wearable technology to monitor pet activity and health.']}], 'design_principles': [{'principle': 'The system should integrate mental, emotional, and physical health aspects to provide a holistic approach to pet care.', 'insight_id': 'Holistic Pet Care: A Reflection of Societal Shifts in Health and Wellness', 'action_verbs': ['integrate', 'provide'], 'design_direction': 'Holistic Health Integration', 'priority': 0.9, 'feasibility': 0.8}, {'principle': 'The experience must prioritize preventive care measures over reactive treatments to promote long-term pet health.', 'insight_id': 'Proactive Pet Healthcare: A Paradigm Shift from Treatment to Prevention', 'action_verbs': ['prioritize', 'promote'], 'design_direction': 'Preventive Care Focus', 'priority': 0.9, 'feasibility': 0.75}, {'principle': 'The system should offer customization options for pet nutrition and exercise plans to match individual health needs.', 'insight_id': 'Customized Pet Nutrition and Exercise: Tailoring Health to Individual Needs', 'action_verbs': ['offer', 'match'], 'design_direction': 'Customization for Individual Needs', 'priority': 0.85, 'feasibility': 0.7}], 'current_step': 'completed', 'messages': [AIMessage(content='Created 11 chunks using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Generated 11 inferences using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Identified 3 patterns using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Generated 3 insights using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='Created 3 design principles using LangChain output parser', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={})], 'analysis_metadata': {'request_id': 'd216fbce-82af-4e46-8427-2ba25b1e4ade', 'framework': 'Hybrid (LangGraph + OpenAI Agentic)', 'model': 'gpt-4-turbo-preview', 'orchestration': 'LangGraph', 'function_calling': 'OpenAI Native', 'research_data_s3_path': 'research_data/aas-1-1.txt'}}
